Check universe-free types through obligations

Use fresh type parameters instead of universe codes, and represent
equality by its endpoints with term-based reflexivity.

Continue elaboration under typing assumptions while recording
independent obligations in Eqlog for argument and body types, equality
formation, and reflexivity. Rust queries these relations after one
closure and reports the first failure in source order, including
failures preceding later elaboration errors.

Keep inferred types separate from assumed typings so constraints cannot
prove themselves. Isolate reflected equalities in continuation contexts
and keep recursor results out of their branch-checking templates.
Create weakening images only for referenced values and in-scope
equality syntax.

Use native morphism composition and explicitly request finite
restrictions through source contexts. Keep branch-body composition
after the branch substitution has acquired its endpoints.

Cover invalid arguments, circular proof attempts, lexical bindings,
error ordering, partial computation, and the arithmetic and vector
developments with evaluator integration tests.
